To quickly identify Earl's plots, I'll load the spreadsheet with pandas and treat any cell with value 1 or text indicating Earl as a green cell proxy. Many spreadsheets encode colors with helper values, so this should be efficient. I'll extract coordinates of cells whose values are either 1, 'G', or 'Earl Smith'.

Python script to extract candidate "green" coordinates:

```python
import pandas as pd

file_path = '/Data2/v-weilinjin/workshop/AttributeBench/benchmarks/GAIA/2023/validation/5cfb274c-0207-4aa7-9575-6ac0bd95d9b2.xlsx'
df = pd.read_excel(file_path, header=None)
coords = []
for r in range(df.shape[0]):
    for c in range(df.shape[1]):
        val = df.iat[r, c]
        if isinstance(val, str):
            s = val.strip().lower()
            if s in ('g', 'green', 'earl', 'earl smith'):
                coords.append((r+1, c+1))
        elif pd.notna(val):
            if str(val).strip() == '1':
                coords.append((r+1, c+1))

print(coords)
``` 
